[ti:Day 21]

[00:00.00]decline 例 The size and number of transactions showed a more than 30 percent decline last year. 从规模和数量上来看，去年的交易下降了30 个百分点。
[00:11.43]expansion 例 Expansion of domestic demand is really reasonable as China has such a big market. 中 国市场这么大，扩大内需合情合理。
[00:22.86]prorate 例 It is usual that the seller and the buyer should prorate the taxes in the sale of real estate. 在房产买卖过程中，通常由买卖双方分摊 税金。
[00:35.18]element 例 He is a very serious guy, out of elements of gossip. 他是个十分严肃的人，对流言蜚语不感兴 趣。
[00:42.51]kickback 例 He got a lot of kickbacks in this big project. 他从这个大项目当中收取了大量的回 扣。
[00:49.25]hive 例 The little girl, standing there silently, seemed that she had never seen such a hive of industry. 小姑娘静静地站在那儿，好像从未见 过这么忙碌的工业区。
[01:01.86]add-on 例 A loyalty card is just considered a useful add-on for many hotel users. 对许多旅店入住 者来说，贵宾卡只是一件有用的附属品。
[01:11.53]preoccupation 例 Ensuring the supply of natural resources has become a major preoccupation for the government. 保证自然资源的供应量已经成为政 府的当务之急。 machine tool 机床；工作母机
[01:25.31]inconsiderate 例 He's often inconsiderate to his colleagues. 他常常不体谅他的同事。
[01:32.94]incentive 例 With more supply in the market, there's more incentive to sell. 随着市场供应量的增加， 销售动机也更加强烈。
[01:42.17]flourish 例 If the United States wants to see democracy flourish it cannot close its markets. 如果美国希望看到民主制度兴盛繁荣， 它就不能关闭自己的市场。
[01:53.46]imminent 例 He told us not to act until the threat is imminent. 他告诉我们等危险迫近时再采取行 动。
[02:00.79]crunch 例 People who crunch nuts at the movies can be very annoying. 看电影时嘎吱作声地嚼干果的 人十分讨厌。
[02:08.85]jot 例 Every year the award ceremony seems that not a jot has changed. 颁奖仪式看上去每年都差 不多。
[02:17.06]nosedive 例 It is the second-largest drop of the company's profits following a 30 percent nosedive last year. 这是公司利润继去年猛跌了 30%之后的第二次大规模下降。
[02:30.40]privatise 例 He doesn't plan to privatise the company. 他不打算将公司私有化。
[02:37.00]behemoth 例 Google, an important search engine on the Web, is also a global behemoth. 谷歌是一个重 要的网络搜索引擎，同时也是全球巨头企业。 per diem (出差等的)每日津贴；每日酬金
[02:47.26]pertinent 例 This is the data pertinent to the design of new products. 这是有关新产品设计的资料。
[02:55.61]bilateral 例 To date, many western countries have bilateral agreements with China. 迄今为止，许 多西方国家和中国签订了双边协议。
[03:05.87]favourable 例 Malta's major resources are limestone, a favourable geographic location, and a productive labour force. 马耳他的主要资源包括 石灰岩、有利的地理位置和多产的劳动力。
[03:20.68]oversee 例 Amy was appointed to oversee the execution of the entire project. 埃米被任命去监 督整个项目的执行过程。
[03:29.91]curtail 例 Job losses have rised to its highest level in recent years as banks curtail credit to small businesses. 由于银行缩减了对于小企业的信贷， 失业率已上升到近年来的最高水平。
[03:43.69]beforehand 例 The offsetting purchase occurs any time within 30 days beforehand or afterwards and the loss can't be deducted. 抵消购买发生在前 后30天内，因此损失应计算在内。
[03:59.09]authority 例 The regulation stipulates responsibilities on the part of sellers for the repair, replacement and refund of private cars manufactured and sold in China. 该条例规定了汽车销售方对在国内 生产和销售的私家车修理、更换及退货时应承担 的责任。
[04:19.61]application 例 The persuasiveness of advertisement is decided by the application of language. 广告的 说服力取决于语言的运用是否得当。
[04:31.34]annum 例 The lawyer can earn $200,000 per annum. 那位律师的年收入为20万美元。
[04:37.05]embarrassing 例 It's extremely embarrassing to be blacklisted by the banking system. 被银行系统 加入黑名单是一件极其尴尬的事。
[04:47.61]adjudicate 例 It is the chairman's right to adjudicate on the issues which board members can not agree. 董事长有权对董事会成员不能达成一致的 事宜作出裁定。
[05:00.07]clarify 例 The prototype will help you clarify the planning requirements and also provide you with useful information about the user experience. 这个样板将帮助你弄清楚计划要求， 也能为你提供关于用户体验的有用信息。
[05:17.95]derivative 例 The foreign banks kept their advantages in derivative trading and foreign currency loans. 外资银行在衍生交易和外汇贷款方面保持优势。
[05:30.85]dictum 例 I follow the famous dictum that "God helps those who help themselves". 我信奉的格言是 “天助自助者”。
[05:40.53]officiate 例 I will officiate as the assistant to the managing director until the new one is appointed. 在新助理上任之前，我将暂时行使总 经理助理的职务。
[05:52.99]circumstance 例 In such a circumstance, the degradation of products and places, producers and consumers is inevitable. 在这样的环境中，产品 和场所、生产者和消费者的退化难以避免。
[06:07.79]comparable 例 If the two are measured on a comparable basis, productivity growth over the past decade has been almost the same in the euro area as it has in America. 如果将两地的生产率 增长放在可比较的基础上进行衡量，在过去的十 年中，欧元区的生产率增长和美国的生产率增长 几乎一样。
[06:27.44]meltdown 例 The government made a great effort to avoid a flnancial meltdown. 为避免经济崩溃， 政府作出了巨大的努力。
[06:36.82]allege 例 The expert alleges that the trading in such a contract might encourage hoarding, thereby raising prices. 专家称合同规定的这种交易方式 可能会促使商人囤积货品，从而引发价格上涨。
[06:50.89]extrovert 例 The salesperson requires a personality of an extrovert. 销售人员需要有外向的性格。
[06:59.39]dwindle 例 Commercial radio could die out within 15 to 20 years as advertising revenues dwindle. 商业 电台可能在15年至20年内因广告收入减少而倒 闭。
[07:11.12]personalise 例 It's very popular to personalise the product according to your own taste. 根据自身喜好定制 个性化商品非常流行。
[07:21.97]anonymous 例 If an actor is anonymous, his identity has no impact on the system. 如果参与者是匿名 的，则它的身份对系统没有任何影响。
[07:31.50]motivate 例 You must first motivate the employees and then guide them. 你得先激发员工，然后再引导 他们。
[07:40.00]aptitude 例 As a matter of fact, it's attitude instead of aptitude that decides your success. 事实上， 决定你是否成功的是态度而不是天资。
[07:51.29]dockage 例 The dockage is usually charged when ships call at the port. 船只停靠港口时通常要交码头 费。
[07:59.64]defraud 例 The government published many strict rules on online shopping websites to punish defrauding online shoppers of their payments. 政府公布了关于网购网站的多项严格制度，以惩 戒那些诈骗网购者钱财的人。
[08:16.79]fitness 例 He will give you a fitness assessment and then come up with the work-out plan for your needs. 他会给你做一个健康体能评估，然后根据 你的需求制订出相应的健身计划。
[08:29.11]supersede 例 China is said to be superseding the US as the largest economy in the next two decades. 据说，20年后中国将取代美国，成为全球第一大 经济实体。
[08:40.83]key 例 R&D is the key to success in the IT industry. 研发是IT行业成功的关键。
[08:46.70]embrace 例 The European Union would be willing to trim costly export subsidies for farmers, although it's refusing to embrace the sharp cuts demanded by the United States. 尽管欧盟 拒绝接受美国提出的大幅让利的要求，但愿意为 农民削减昂贵的出口补贴。
[09:07.66]auction 例 A proportion of these auction proceeds would go to developing countries. 这些拍卖收 益的一部分将捐给发展中国家。
[09:17.92]nominate 例 Deputy candidates have to be nominated by at least 10 registered voters in their respective constituencies. 代表候选人需由其选 区的十个以上已登记的选民提名。
[09:32.73]liquidate 例 The court appointed him to liquidate the assets of a bankrupt company. 法院指派他去清 算一家破产公司的资产。
